    "result": "Perfect! My implementation is complete. Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary of Implementation\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` following test-driven development principles. Here's what was added:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n1. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`** - Enhanced `generateReport`:\n   - Accepts optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`)\n   - Evaluates each threshold against metric scores\n   - Marks threshold as failed if score is null or below minimum\n   - Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` array to report when thresholds provided\n   - Maintains backward compatibility - without thresholds, report structure unchanged\n\n2. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`** - Enhanced Markdown reporter:\n   - Adds \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL for each threshold\n   - Displays metric ID, minimum, actual score\n\n3. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`** - Comprehensive test coverage:\n   - Tests threshold passing/failing logic\n   - Tests handling of missing scores (null)\n   - Tests multiple thresholds\n   - Tests both JSON and Markdown report output\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n4. **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`** - Added threshold support:\n   - New `--threshold <metric>=<number>` option (repeatable)\n   - `parseThresholdStrings()` - Validates format and 0-1 range\n   - `validateAndBuildThresholds()` - Validates against available metrics\n   - Exit behavior: 0 if pass/no thresholds, 1 if fail, 2 for errors\n   - Works with custom metrics via dynamic validation\n\n5. **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.test.ts`** - Unit tests for parsing logic\n\n### Documentation\n\n6. **`README.md`** - Added `--threshold` option documentation\n7. **`docs/eval_harness_design.md`** - Documented threshold feature design\n8. **`examples/eval-with-thresholds.js`** - Example showing SDK usage\n\n### Exit Codes\n- **0**: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)\n- **1**: Any threshold fails\n- **2**: Malformed threshold or unknown metric ID (with helpful error messages)\n\nThe implementation fully supports custom metrics and maintains backward compatibility.",
